.TH AENIGMA-VPN-DNS 8 "2026-08-17" "aenigma 5.0.0" "Aenigma Administration Scripts"
.SH NAME
aenigma-vpn-dns \- configure DNS resolution and push directives for a VPN server instance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aenigma-vpn-dns
.B \-d
.I DOMAIN
.B \-i
.I DNS_IP
.B \-f
.I INTERFACE
.RB [ \-c
.IR CNAME ]
.br
.B aenigma-vpn-dns
.B \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aenigma-vpn-dns
installs and configures
.BR dnsmasq (8)
to serve DNS over a VPN tunnel interface for a server instance previously
provisioned by
.BR aenigma-vpn-server (8),
and adds the corresponding
.B dhcp-option
push directives to that instance's OpenVPN server configuration so
connecting clients receive the pushed DNS server and search domain.
.PP
A per-instance
.BR dnsmasq (8)
configuration is written to
.IB /etc/dnsmasq.d/ DOMAIN .conf ,
bound to the given
.I INTERFACE
and backed by a per-instance hosts file. That hosts file is not populated
by this script; individual client hostname entries are added to it by
.BR aenigma-vpn-server-host (8).
If
.B \-c
.I CNAME
is given, this script additionally adds a
.B cname
directive making
.I DOMAIN
resolve as an alias for
.IR CNAME .
.PP
.B aenigma-vpn-dns
must be run as root, since it installs packages, writes into
.I /etc/dnsmasq.d
and the target instance's OpenVPN configuration, and restarts the
.B dnsmasq
and
.B openvpn@
services.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-d " DOMAIN"
Name of the VPN server instance to configure DNS for (as passed to
.BR aenigma-vpn-server (8)
via its
.B \-d
option). Required.
.TP
.BI \-i " DNS_IP"
Address to push to clients as their DNS server, typically the VPN
server's own tunnel address, e.g.
.IR 10.8.0.1 .
Required.
.TP
.BI \-f " INTERFACE"
Network interface
.BR dnsmasq (8)
should bind to and serve DNS on, e.g.
.IR tun0 .
Required.
.TP
.BI \-c " CNAME"
Optional. If given, makes
.I DOMAIN
resolve as a
.BR dnsmasq (8)
.B cname
alias for this target, instead of relying on a direct hosts-file entry.
.TP
.B \-h
Display usage information and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; DNS was configured and the
.B dnsmasq
and
.B openvpn@
services were restarted.
.TP
.B 1
Invoked without root privileges, called with insufficient or invalid
arguments, or the target VPN server instance has not been provisioned
(its configuration file was not found).
.SH FILES
.TP
.IB /etc/openvpn/ DOMAIN .conf
Target server instance's OpenVPN configuration. Must already exist,
created by
.BR aenigma-vpn-server (8).
.B dhcp-option DOMAIN
and
.B dhcp-option DNS
push directives are added or refreshed here.
.TP
.IB /etc/dnsmasq.d/ DOMAIN .conf
Generated
.BR dnsmasq (8)
configuration for this instance, fully rewritten on every run.
.TP
.IB /etc/openvpn/ DOMAIN /dnsmasq-hosts
Per-instance hosts file referenced via
.B addn-hosts
in the generated
.BR dnsmasq (8)
configuration. Created empty if missing; populated separately by
.BR aenigma-vpn-server-host (8).
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Both the
.B dhcp-option DOMAIN
and
.B dhcp-option DNS
push directives in the target server configuration are unconditionally
removed and re-added on every run, rather than added only if not already
present. This means re-running
.B aenigma-vpn-dns
with a different
.I DNS_IP
always reflects the new value, and a directive that was manually commented
out between runs is restored to active rather than silently left disabled.
.IP \(bu 2
The generated
.BR dnsmasq (8)
configuration file is fully rewritten on each run, so changing
.I INTERFACE
or adding/removing
.B \-c
.I CNAME
between runs takes effect cleanly without leftover directives from a
previous run.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aenigma-vpn-server (8),
.BR aenigma-vpn-server-host (8),
.BR dnsmasq (8),
.BR openvpn (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Romulus-Emanuel Ruja <romulus.rujas@aenigma.ro>